Dear {!Contact.FirstName}, 

A proficiency examination can satisfy a student’s foreign language graduation requirement.

The student must demonstrate proficiency at the fourth semester intermediate level and must pass with a grade of "C"  or better in order to test out of the requirement. Only one opportunity to test out of the language requirement is allowed. Students who do not pass will be required to take the appropriate level language course(s) to satisfy the language requirement for their degree. 

Students who wish to test for French, German, or Spanish proficiency must take a CLEP test. To access the application for CLEP, please visit: https://uoeee.asu.edu/exam/clep. For all other languages, please complete the Proficiency Examination Application online at: http://silc.asu.edu/testing/undergraduate/language_proficiency  

Please note that native speakers who have completed all of their high school or college subjects and coursework in the language to be tested may not need to take an exam. Please contact your academic advisor or the Language Proficiency Coordinator (Barbara.Fleming@asu.edu) for more information. 

Language Proficiency Exam dates for Fall  2016

Wednesday, September 14th, noon- 3:30 pm

Monday, October 3rd,  9am to noon

Friday, November 4th, 9am to noon

Students must submit a proficiency exam application and receive a testing confirmation email in order to test on these dates: https://clas-forms.asu.edu/silc/language-proficiency-examination-application

If you have further questions, please email silctesting@asu.edu.

Best regards,